# Beyond the Stars - SHOWCASE v2 (docs/recording.md). The post-UEV game: the Eye and its automation, extraction, the
# harder stars, the Kerr, the Homogeny and Reality machines, the quasar and the conduit, the Eye's galaxy tiers, how a
# player builds one, the quest book. About 7 minutes at 1920x1080, 30 fps.
#
# Honesty rules this script keeps:
# - Every site is raised by script in a fresh creative superflat world; captions say "set up by script" for anything
#   placed, filled or set by a command (milestones, cores handed in, creative power, supply tanks).
# - What runs after that runs on its own: the AE2 rigs, the standard gate rig (it reads only the Eye's Directive
#   Hatches; /btseye star ... liverig), the quasar rig (it reads only the Directive Hatches and drives the Burst Control
#   Hatches with redstone; /btsquasar autorig ... 0 eye ...; the collapse cue, Galaxy Transition [4], runs over a GT
#   wireless redstone cover pair from the Eye's hatch to the quasar's Burst Control Hatch, P4-95), the machines
#   themselves.
# - Screens are the controller GUI kit's (B-96..B-101, B-115, B-116): no scanner side panels.
# - Long stretches run under the time warp (/btswarp, a cheat: the whole server runs N ticks per real tick through the
#   normal code). Its tag shows the measured multiplier and the game time; a time-lapse tag shows frame sampling.
#
# On master the questbook carries the UXV / MAX / Endgame chapters; -Dbts.rec.questsdir=<a DefaultQuests tree> still
# points the client at another one.
#
# Sites (z 4000, all facing north): Rig B, the Kerr on AE2 (x 1700); Rig C, the AE2 Eye (x 2400); the climbing Eye
# (x 3000, kit T6 set back to a dark T1); the build-logic Eye (x 3300); the tier Eye (x 3600); the Kerr tiers
# (x 5000 / 5130); the Homogeny (x 6600), Reality Diffraction (x 6900), Reality Refab (x 7150); the conduit rig and its
# quasar (x 8000-8270, y 100); the galaxy Eye (x 10000) and its quasar (x 10000, y 100, z 4400).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- setup (never recorded)
time day
command /btsquests install
build eyeae
build kerr
points keectrl
terminal 2394,5,3996 side north name ae.term
# the climbing Eye: kit to T6 (every band and generator), then back to a dark T1 with empty buses
kit eye 6 3000,5,4000 gen 5 name climb
menet climb
points climb
command /btseye star {climb} rig none
command /btseye star {climb} unlock 1
command /btseye star {climb} buses clear
command /btseye star {climb} target sol
command /btseye star {climb} fill
# the tier Eye (tier 1 with tier-6 generators, so the projector can add each band) and the Kerr tiers
kit eye 1 3600,5,4000 gen 5 name tiers
kit kerr t1 5130,36,4000 name kt1
kit kerr t2 5000,36,4000 name kt2
# the Homogeny (T1) on creative power, Reality Diffraction and Refab
command /btshr homogeny t1 6600 40 4000 north fill
command /btshr keep homogeny 6600 40 4000 north t2
name hom 6600,40,4000
creativepower hom
command /btshr diffraction 6900 8 4000 north fill
command /btshr keep diffraction 6900 8 4000 north
name dif 6900,8,4000
command /btshr refab 7150 6 4000 north fill
command /btshr keep refab 7150 6 4000 north
name ref 7150,6,4000
# the conduit rig: a quasar with a crown on its top port, a Wormhole Mouth pair from its bottom port, two Mirrors, a
# Junction, a remote crown and two receptor ports
command /btsconduit rig 8000 100 4000
name cq 8000,100,4000
name cq.c 8000,115,4072
name crown 7988,196,4072
name moutha 8000,34,4089
name mouthb 8100,43,4067
name mirror1 8102,55,4123
name junction 8191,75,4128
name mirror2 8265,62,4133
name rcrown 8258,96,4116
# the galaxy Eye (kit T8, dark) and its quasar (unseeded: the seeding is filmed)
kit eye 8 10000,5,4000 gen 8 name gal
command /btsquasar t3 10000 100 4400 north
command /btsquasar keep 10000 100 4400
name gq 10000,100,4400
name gq.c 10000,115,4472

# ================================================================ title
scene title
  card 4 Beyond the Stars | Post-UEV: stars, black holes, quasars and the machines that run them | a GregTech: New Horizons 2.9 addon - recorded in game

# ================================================================ 1. The Eye and its automation
scene c1
  card 3 1. The Eye and its automation | an Eye of Harmony that feeds and holds its own star

scene ae-intro
  caption An Eye of Harmony, tier 1, fed and held by AE2 alone: no hand on it, no GT covers, one redstone dust per bus. Built by script in a fresh creative world.
  orbit aeeye+0,-10,0 radius 100 height 32 from -55 to 35 seconds 8

scene ae-core
  caption The main ME network (orange) stocks the Eye's gas and ignition charges and takes its products.
  goto ae.core+-4,4,-8 look ae.core+-4,0,1
  label ae.tankhe side left | Gas supply: endless test tanks behind read-only storage buses, standing in for your production (set up by script)
  label ae.drive side up | ME drive: ignition charges, room for the products
  label ae.emitter side right | Level emitter: lamp lit while a charge is in stock
  hold 5

scene ae-trim
  caption The trims have their own network. A Directive Hatch reads the star's field every second; while it wants Helium its bit is on, one dust carries it to an export bus, and the bus pushes Helium into the Field hatch.
  goto ae.trimhe.cam look ae.trimhe+0,0.5,0
  label ae.dirhe side up | Directive Hatch, Trims, Bit 1: pressure too high
  label ae.trimhe side left | AE2 fluid export bus with a redstone card
  label ae.fieldhe side down | Field hatch (LV, so the bus cannot stockpile)
  hold 6

scene ae-light
  caption The supply opens and the charge cell goes into the drive (set up by script). From here nothing touches the Eye: it fills its buffers, takes a charge and lights its star itself.
  goto aeeye+0,-14,-88 look aeeye+0,-6,0
  aecells
  warp 6
  timelapse 20 speed 1 until aelit tail 3
  command /btseye star {aeeyectrl} status
  melist ae.term

scene ae-burn
  caption Sol is burning. The trim buses switch on and off to hold the field; Raw Star Matter flows into the network every 60 s cycle.
  warp 20
  orbit aeeye+0,-8,0 radius 80 height 20 from 30 to -30 seconds 8

scene eye-gui
  caption The controller screen: the star and its zone, each gauge against its band, the upkeep and buffers, and the trim the field wants next. The side panels hold the field's detail and the Info page.
  goto aeeyectrl+0,0.2,-3.5 look aeeyectrl
  gui aeeyectrl
  warp 20
  hold 6
  close

scene eye-t1
  caption Eye tiers. Tier 1 is the core: plinth, band and field generators (19,616 blocks). Each tier adds a band and a harder star. (Raised by the dev kit, its generators already at tier 6.)
  goto tiers.c+-80,30,-80 look tiers.c+0,-8,0
  hold 4

scene eye-t2
  caption Tier 2 adds the beam band: Sirius A. Then the jet crescent (tier 3, Arcturus)...
  hologram tiers survival tier 2 budget 9 every 1 tail 0.5 max 10
  hologram tiers survival tier 3 budget 9 every 1 tail 0.5 max 10

scene eye-t4
  caption ...the spiral arms (tier 4, the neutron star), the second arms (tier 5, Sirius B)...
  goto tiers.c+-112,44,-112 look tiers.c+0,-8,0
  hologram tiers survival tier 4 budget 14 every 1 tail 0.5 max 10
  hologram tiers survival tier 5 budget 14 every 1 tail 0.5 max 10

scene eye-t6
  caption ...and the galactic rim (tier 6, the magnetar). Each tier also needs its compression generators and a core; a tier above a recipe's own doubles its parallel.
  hologram tiers survival tier 6 budget 22 every 1 tail 1 max 12
  orbit tiers.c+0,-8,0 radius 165 height 50 from -45 to 20 seconds 5

# ================================================================ 2. Extraction
scene c2
  card 3 2. Extraction | what the star makes, and how it leaves the Eye

scene ext-me
  caption The Eye's products come out of an ME output hatch and bus straight into the network: here Sol's Raw Star Matter, about 62,500 L every cycle, counted by the ME terminal.
  goto ae.term+0,0.6,-2.6 look ae.term
  use ae.term side north
  warp 40
  hold 9
  close

scene ext-tiers
  card 5 What each tier makes | T1 Sol: Raw Star Matter  -  T2 Sirius A: Excited Stellar Plasma  -  T3 Arcturus: Hyperdense Plasma | T4 neutron star: White Dwarf Matter  -  T5 Sirius B: Black Dwarf Matter  -  T6 magnetar: Magnetar Matter | T7 Triangulum: Ergomatter  -  T8 Milky Way: Superdense Ergomatter | (the next chapter's Eye sends each into its own ME network)

# ================================================================ 3. The harder stars
scene c3
  card 3 3. The harder stars | one Eye climbs from Sol to a magnetar, run by its Directive Hatches

scene hs-intro
  caption This Eye was raised to tier 6 by the dev kit and set back to a dark tier 1. Each tier's milestones (hours of play) are set done by script, one at a time. Everything else is the standard rig: once a second it reads only the Eye's Directive Hatches and opens the matching valve.
  command /btseye star {climb} liverig on
  goto climb.c+0,25,-45 look climb.c
  warp 40
  timelapse 6 speed 1 until lit:climb tail 3

scene hs-t2
  caption T1 -> T2, the Mass Infusion (milestones set by script). The rig hands in the Stellar Mass Core and the Sirius A chart when the Transition hatch asks; the infusion takes 600 s.
  command /btseye star {climb} milestones 1 done
  goto climb+0,0.2,-3.5 look climb
  gui climb
  warp 40
  timelapse 14 speed 2 until unlocked:climb:2 tail 1 clock
  close

scene hs-t3
  caption T2 -> T3, the Shell Ignition (milestones set by script): its forced helium flash is ridden on the Status hatch's event bit. Arcturus burns.
  command /btseye star {climb} milestones 2 done
  goto climb.c+0,25,-45 look climb.c
  warp 40
  timelapse 14 speed 2 until unlocked:climb:3 tail 1 clock

scene hs-t4
  caption T3 -> T4, the Core Collapse (milestones set by script): the Transition hatch asks for Tachyon for its 940 s, the rig opens the valve, and Arcturus collapses into a neutron star.
  command /btseye star {climb} milestones 3 done
  goto climb+0,0.2,-3.5 look climb
  gui climb
  warp 40
  timelapse 14 speed 3 until unlocked:climb:4 tail 1 clock
  close

scene hs-neutron
  caption T4, the neutron star: three gauges now (pressure P, temperature, spin), polar beams, and a Feed - the HSM you feed it sets its White Dwarf Matter. Four trims, one per Trims bit: Space, SpaceTime, Super Coolant, Tengam.
  goto climb.c+0,25,-45 look climb.c
  warp 20
  hold 5
  goto climb+0,0.2,-3.5 look climb
  gui climb
  hold 6
  close

scene hs-cooling
  caption T4 -> T5, the First Cooling (milestones set by script): Sirius B cools in 7,200 s batches. The setpoint runs from +90 to -90; at the crystallisation plateau the screen warns ahead, and the batch must keep a mean Y of 0.9 to count.
  command /btseye star {climb} milestones 4 done
  goto climb+0,0.2,-3.5 look climb
  gui climb
  warp 60
  timelapse 30 speed 10 until unlocked:climb:5 tail 1 clock
  close

scene hs-merger
  caption T5 -> T6, the Magnetar Merger (milestones set by script): the dynamo winds the field up; held +60 to +90 for 120 s, then released. Antipolarization Agent flows on the Status hatch's event bit.
  command /btseye star {climb} milestones 5 done
  goto climb+0,0.2,-3.5 look climb
  gui climb
  warp 20
  timelapse 12 speed 2 until unlocked:climb:6 tail 2 clock
  close

scene hs-agent
  caption T6, the magnetar: giant flares every 60-120 s, warned 15 s ahead. Status bit 3 says "Agent wanted"; the rig's Agent valve answers it, and the shield holds.
  goto climb.dir.eye_status+0,1,-3 look climb.dir.eye_status
  gui climb.dir.eye_status
  warp 10
  hold 6
  close
  goto climb.c+50,35,-70 look climb.c
  warp 20
  hold 3
  goto climb.c+0,25,-45 look climb.c
  hold 3

scene hs-products
  caption Its ME network after the climb, filled by the ME output hatch and bus with no hand on it: Raw Star Matter, Excited Stellar Plasma and the Purified Tengam the magnetar gives back. (On this scripted climb the higher stars burned only minutes each.)
  goto climb.termcam look climb.term
  use climb.term side north
  warp 20
  hold 5
  close
  melist climb.term

# ================================================================ 4. The Kerr
scene c4
  card 3 4. The Kerr | a black hole fed by AE2

scene kerr-rig
  caption The Kerr Ergosphere Engine, tier 1, on AE2: one Directive Hatch per job, each switching an export bus on demand.
  goto k.core+0,7,-22 look k.core+0,-2,8
  label k.boltdir side up | Directive Hatch, Hole Bit 3: the bolt stock runs short
  label k.boltbus side right | Export bus: SpaceTime bolts into the bolt bus
  label k.seedbus side left | Export bus: a Black Hole Seed while the hole is closed
  hold 6

scene kerr-run
  caption The cell of bolts and seeds goes into the drive (set up by script). The network seeds the hole, then feeds it bolts as it climbs to its setpoint.
  goto kerr+60,18,-70 look kerr
  cell
  warp 30
  orbit kerr radius 90 height 22 from -40 to 40 seconds 10

scene kerr-gui
  caption The Kerr's screen: the hole's mass against its setpoint, the bolt stock, the modules.
  goto keectrl+0,0.2,-3.5 look keectrl
  gui keectrl
  warp 10
  hold 5
  close

scene kerr-extract
  caption The Kerr Extractor Module runs GT's extractor recipes off the open hole: linked to it, the hole's mass sets its parallels and speed (448, x4 here). Its input bus is stocked by script with 1,024 Stemcells: it starts on its own and takes them all in one 1.7 s run.
  warp off
  goto keectrl.modx+0,0.2,-3.5 look keectrl.modx
  gui keectrl.modx
  command /btskerr module {keectrl} x stock 0 longest 16
  hold 5
  close
  command /btskerr module {keectrl} x status

scene kerr-tiers
  caption Kerr tiers side by side. Tier 2, with the Kerr Density Upgrade: setpoint up to 512 solar masses, and Kerr Densification in the Compressor Module.
  label kt1.c side up | Tier 1
  label kt2.c side up | Tier 2
  goto 5150,58,3895 look 5150,30,4040
  dolly 5150,58,3895 4980,58,3895 seconds 7

# ================================================================ 5. Homogeny and Reality
scene c5
  card 3 5. The Homogeny and the Reality machines | mixing star matter, and what comes after

scene hom-t1
  caption The Homogeny, tier 1, mixing Raw Star Matter into Excited Stellar Plasma Mixture (built by its bench, on creative power: set up by script).
  goto hom+-40,40,-60 look hom+0,0,30
  hold 3
  goto hom+0,4,-6 look hom
  gui hom
  warp 20
  hold 4
  close

scene hom-ring
  caption Tier 2 needs the stirring ring, built here by the projector's survival auto-place...
  goto hom+-40,40,-60 look hom+0,0,30
  hologram hom survival tier 2 budget 6 every 1 tail 1 max 15

scene hom-install
  caption ...the 100,000 L milestone (set by script) and the Tier II core handed in (by script). Install runs 600 s offline; then T2: four parallels and Degenerate Stellar Mixture.
  command /btshr bench {hom} project 2
  creativepower hom
  command /btshr bench {hom} milestone 100000 0
  command /btshr bench {hom} escrow
  command /btshr bench {hom} on
  command /btshr bench {hom} install
  goto hom+0,4,-6 look hom
  gui hom
  warp 40
  timelapse 22 speed 2 until game:1000 tail 1 clock
  hold 2
  close
  command /btshr bench {hom} on
  command /btshr bench {hom} status

scene reality
  caption Reality Diffraction, formed by its bench with its inputs filled by script. It is not running here: it needs a Bose-Einstein network with a Containment Field, which this test world does not have. Its screen's checklist says so.
  goto dif+0,6,-30 look dif+0,20,30
  hold 3
  goto dif+0,0.2,-3.5 look dif
  gui dif
  hold 4
  close

scene refab
  caption Reality Refab is not running either: its regions come only from a running Diffraction, through the same BEC network. Both are the ladder's next part (MAX); its screen lists what it waits for.
  goto ref+0,10,-40 look ref+0,40,30
  hold 3
  goto ref+0,0.2,-3.5 look ref
  gui ref
  hold 4
  close

# ================================================================ 6. The Quasar and the Conduit
scene c6
  card 3 6. The Quasar and the Conduit | a quasar's jets carried across the world

scene q-seed
  caption Seeding a Quasar Engine: a Quasar Seed in the slot and Open (done by script, as the GUI's button). A 64 solar-mass hole lights its disc. (It is then grown to 136 solar masses by script; from here the quasar rig runs it, for chapter 7.)
  goto gq+0,0.2,-3.5 look gq
  command /btsquasar seed {gq}
  gui gq
  warp 4
  timelapse 8 speed 1 until game:30 tail 1
  close
  command /btsquasar feed {gq} 1.0
  command /btsquasar mass {gq} 136
  # the quasar rig takes the quasar now, so its disc has settled (trims, purges) by chapter 7; the Eye is dark
  command /btseye star {gal} unlock 6
  command /btsquasar autorig {gq} 0 eye {gal}

scene q-disc
  caption The disc: its energy E, flux and the hole's mass and spin. Flux builds until it erupts on its own; a purge (the Burst Control Hatch, a redstone edge) vents it early.
  goto cq+0,0.2,-3.5 look cq
  gui cq
  warp 20
  hold 6
  close

scene q-jets
  caption Inside the shell, in the open chamber around the hole: the disc and the two jets, which leave through the caps (top: a Burst Thermaliser Crown; bottom: a Wormhole Mouth). A purge (set off by script, as the Purge button) flashes the disc.
  goto cq.c+0,6,-24 look cq.c
  warp 10
  hold 3
  command /btsquasar purge {cq}
  hold 3
  goto cq.c+-18,-6,-18 look cq.c+0,6,0
  hold 3

scene conduit
  caption The Conduit: the mouth under the quasar is paired with one 100 blocks away; the stream comes out of its back into a Mirror, which turns it into a Junction that splits it three ways.
  goto mouthb+-40,50,-90 look mirror1
  hold 3
  goto moutha+0,0.2,-3.5 look moutha
  gui moutha
  hold 3
  close
  goto junction+0,0.2,-3.5 look junction
  gui junction
  hold 4
  close

scene crown
  caption Burst Thermaliser Crown: every Bu/t of the stream becomes 10^13 EU/t, straight into the owner's wireless network.
  goto crown+0,0.2,-3.5 look crown
  gui crown
  warp 10
  hold 5
  close

scene receptor
  caption GRB Receptor Ports feed a host: this crown is fed by Mirror 2 through its port, 150 blocks from the quasar.
  goto rcrown+0,0.2,-3.5 look rcrown
  gui rcrown
  hold 5
  close

# ================================================================ 7. Eye T7-T8
scene c7
  card 3 7. Eye T7 and T8 | a magnetar becomes a galaxy

scene gal-collapse
  caption An Eye at T6 (its milestones set done by script) on the real quasar from chapter 6. The quasar rig reads only the Directive Hatches; the collapse cue runs over a GT wireless redstone pair to the quasar's Burst Control Hatch, 2 s ahead, so the 3 s eruption lands on the collapse second.
  command /btseye star {gal} unlock 6
  command /btseye star {gal} fill
  command /btseye star {gal} target magnetar
  command /btseye star {gal} lit magnetar
  command /btseye star {gal} milestones 6 done
  command /btseye star {gal} buses clear
  command /btseye star {gal} rig none
  goto gal+0,0.2,-3.5 look gal
  gui gal
  warp 60
  timelapse 30 speed 4 until unlocked:gal:7 tail 1 clock
  close
  command /btsquasar autorig status

scene gal-t7
  caption T7, Triangulum: a galaxy of three arms, held on Ergomatter and bursts.
  warp 40
  wait unlocked:gal:7 timeout 600
  goto gal.c+0,55,-35 look gal.c
  warp 20
  hold 5

scene gal-window
  caption From the front at eye level the window in the rim shows the galaxy's core and inner arms; the clamp of the stability rail leaves the opening clear.
  dolly gal.c+0,0.5,-132 gal.c+0,0.5,-98 look gal.c seconds 6
  hold 2

scene gal-merger
  caption T7 -> T8, the Galactic Merger on the same real quasar and rig (Directive codes in, redstone on the Burst Control Hatches out): Begin on the Galaxy Transition hatch, then 1,800 s of pericentre passes. Milestones set done, Supermassive core and Milky Way chart handed in by script.
  command /btseye star {gal} milestones 7 done
  command /btseye star {gal} core supermassive
  command /btseye star {gal} target milkyway
  goto gal+0,0.2,-3.5 look gal
  gui gal
  warp 60
  timelapse 25 speed 4 until unlocked:gal:8 tail 1 clock
  close

scene gal-t8
  caption T8, the Milky Way: four arms and a bar, satellites crossing its disc, Superdense Ergomatter out.
  goto gal.c+0,55,-35 look gal.c
  warp 20
  hold 6

# ================================================================ 8. How to build it
scene c8
  card 3 8. How to build one | hints, auto-place, forming, NEI

scene build-hints
  caption Place the controller and use a Hologram Projector on it: the whole structure appears as hints.
  place bts.eyeOfHarmony 3300,5,4000 facing north name build1
  goto build1+-70,45,-60 look build1+0,10,40
  hologram build1 hints
  hold 3

scene build-survival
  caption Sneak-use it in survival and it places the blocks from your inventory, a batch per use (items supplied by script).
  hologram build1 survival tier 1 budget 10 every 1 tail 1 max 25

scene build-form
  caption With the hatches fitted (here by the dev kit) the controller checks the structure and forms.
  kit eye 1 build1
  goto build1+0,0.2,-3.5 look build1
  gui build1
  hold 4
  close

scene build-nei
  caption NEI shows every multiblock (the structure preview, with tier and layer sliders) and how the controller is made.
  nei usage bts.eyeOfHarmony tab multiblock
  hold 4
  close
  nei recipe bts.eyeOfHarmony
  hold 3
  close

# ================================================================ 9. The quest book
scene c9
  card 3 9. The quest book | the post-UEV chapters (UIV and UMV are the pack's own chapters: not in this dev world)

scene qb-uxv
  caption Tier 13, UXV: the Eye's second half - Sirius B cooling white dwarfs into black ones, the magnetar on Antipolarization Agent - beside the pack's own UXV parts.
  questbook chapter 190:47991
  hold 3
  close

scene qb-max
  caption Tier 14, MAX: the last voltage tier. Our part of it is still to come.
  questbook chapter 190:47992
  hold 3
  close

scene qb-end
  caption The Endgame: what Universium is for, the MHDCSM line, the crafted Stargate.
  questbook chapter 190:47993
  hold 3
  close

# ================================================================ end
scene end
  card 4 Beyond the Stars | Showcase - recorded in a GTNH 2.9 dev client | time warp and bench rigs are dev tools; every run shown is the machines' own
